s for key infrastructure projects: the Bandra (E)-Kalanagar skywalk (almost complete) , the first phase of the Bandra-Dharavi flyover reconstruction (Mithi river widening project ,near completion) , and the Worli connector by December 2026. These projects are expected to improve pedestrian access, ease traffic congestion, and enhance overall connectivity within the city.\n\n## Resale & Rental Listings in Worli Residency\n\nExplore resale and rental listings currently available in Worli Residency, Mumbai.\n\n2 BHK Apartment For Sale in Worli Residency in Kamala Mill, Mumbai\n\nKamala Mill, Mumbai\n\nHemant Sarwan  profile picture\n3 BHK + Servant Room,Study Room Apartment For Sale in Worli Residency in Worli, Mumbai\n\nWorli, Mumbai [...] Rent in Worli Residency ranges from ₹ 66 K to ₹ 12 L with options available for 1 BHK, 2 BHK, 3 BHK, 4 BHK, 5 BHK.\n\nDuring Q2'2026, average property prices for Worli Residency moved from ₹ 76,800/sqft to ₹ 79,300/sqft, reflecting a 3.26% rise.\n\n#### Mumbai to Establish Four New Helipads for Emergency Services\n\nMumbai authorities are planning to construct four new helipads within the next six years to enhance emergency response capabilities. Two helipads will be built along the Coastal Road, one at Worli and another in Kandivali's Charkop area. The remaining two will be developed in the Bandra Kurla Complex (BKC).\n\n#### Elphinstone Road Overbridge Dismantled for Infrastructure Upgrade","score":0.7623715,"raw_content":null,"id":"bc49f3-02"},{"url":"https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/maryland-chs-worli/149477/project","title":"Maryland CHS Worli, Worli, Mumbai - Price on Request","content":"During Q1'2026, average property prices for Maryland CHS Worli moved from ₹ 46,900/sqft to ₹ 51,200/sqft, reflecting a 9.17% rise.\n\n#### Mumbai Infrastructure Projects Gain Momentum with Budget Allocations and Project Launches\n\nMumbai is experiencing a surge in infrastructure and activity. The BMC has proposed a record budget of ₹80,952.56 crore for FY 2026-27, with a significant portion allocated to infrastructure projects like the Coastal Road, Goregaon-Mulund Link Road (GMLR), and Sewage Treatment Plants (STPs).MMRDA has allocated over ₹5,400 crore for road tunnel projects, including one connecting Worli-Bandra Sea Link to Mumbai Airport.\n\n#### BMC Outlines Timelines for Key Infrastructure Projects [...] The BMC has set completion targets for key infrastructure projects: the Bandra (E)-Kalanagar skywalk (almost complete) , the first phase of the Bandra-Dharavi flyover reconstruction (Mithi river widening project ,near completion) , and the Worli connector by December 2026. These projects are expected to improve pedestrian access, ease traffic congestion, and enhance overall connectivity within the city.\n\n## Amenities & Specifications of Maryland CHS Worli\n\n### Sports Sports\n\nSports\n\n### Convenience Convenience\n\nConvenience\n\n### Safety Safety\n\nSafety\n\n### Environment Environment\n\nEnvironment\n\n### Leisure Leisure\n\nLeisure\n\n### Specifications\n\n## Location and Connectivity Around Worli\n\nConnectivity map showing nearby places around Mumbai South [...] During Q2'2026, average property prices for Maryland CHS Worli moved from ₹ 51,200/sqft to ₹ 52,250/sqft, reflecting a 2.05% rise.\n\n#### Mumbai to Establish Four New Helipads for Emergency Services\n\nMumbai authorities are planning to construct four new helipads within the next six years to enhance emergency response capabilities. Two helipads will be built along the Coastal Road, one at Worli and another in Kandivali's Charkop area. The remaining two will be developed in the Bandra Kurla Complex (BKC).\n\n#### Elphinstone Road Overbridge Dismantled for Infrastructure Upgrade","score":0.66308063,"raw_content":null,"id":"69c6ec-03"},{"url":"https://housing.com/in/buy/mumbai/worli-gid/projects","title":"716+ Upcoming Residential Projects in Worli, Mumbai - Housing","content":"Housing.com has 716+ new a